- Current or former smoker with 35-pack-year history;  
- Chronic cough lasting ≥3 months, with sputum production (not dry);  
- Progressive exertional dyspnea severe enough to prevent stair climbing;  
- Unintentional weight loss of 10 lbs over 6 months;  
- Normal spirometry (FEV₁, FVC, FEV₁/FVC all within normal limits);  
- DLCO = 16 mL/min/mmHg — described in summary as “mild-to-moderate reduction”;  
- No hemoptysis, wheeze, chest tightness, purulent sputum, fever, night sweats, clubbing, or other systemic symptoms.

[GAPS]  
- HRCT chest — needed to assess for ground-glass opacities, centrilobular nodules, or mosaic attenuation characteristic of RB-ILD;  
- Bronchoalveolar lavage (BAL) cytology — to identify >20% pigmented macrophages, supportive of RB-ILD;  
- Lung biopsy — gold standard for RB-ILD diagnosis, not performed;  
- Serum alpha-1 antitrypsin level and phenotype — pending;  
- Quantiferon-TB Gold or TST — pending;  
- Sputum AFB smear/culture and NTM PCR — pending.

[DIAGNOSIS]  
Respiratory bronchiolitis–interstitial lung disease (RB-ILD)

